  {"title": [{"text": "Python Trap!", "box": "yellow"}, {"text": "We changed b..."}, {"text": "why did a change?", "box": "red"}],
   "image": {"type": "code", "file": "trap.py",
             "lines": ["a = [1, 2, 3]", "b = a", "b.append(4)", "print(a)"], "highlight": [1]},
   "face": "thinking", "palette": "blue",
   "say": "Look at this Python code. We only add a number to b. So why does a change too?"},
  {"title": [{"text": "The Output", "box": "yellow"}, {"text": "Surprise!", "color": "yellow"}],
   "image": {"type": "code", "file": "trap.py",
             "lines": ["a = [1, 2, 3]", "b = a", "b.append(4)", "print(a)"], "highlight": [3],
             "output": ["[1, 2, 3, 4]"]},
   "face": "worried", "palette": "orange", "reveal": [0.3, 0.4, 0.5, 0.6, 1.2],
   "say": "Run it, and a prints one, two, three, four. Most beginners expect one, two, three."},
  {"title": [{"text": "b = a", "box": "yellow"}, {"text": "is NOT a copy", "box": "red"}],
   "image": {"type": "refs", "names": ["a", "b"], "boxes": [["1", "2", "3"]],
             "links": [[0, 0], [1, 0]], "label": "ONE LIST IN MEMORY"},
   "face": "thinking", "palette": "purple",
   "say": "Here is the reason. b equals a does not copy the list. It gives the same list a second name. Both names point to one list in memory."},
  {"title": [{"text": "One list,", "box": "yellow"}, {"text": "two names"}],
   "image": {"type": "refs", "names": ["a", "b"], "boxes": [["1", "2", "3", "4"]],
             "links": [[0, 0], [1, 0]], "new": [[0, 3]], "label": "ONE LIST IN MEMORY"},
   "face": "worried", "palette": "blue", "reveal": [0.3, 0.6, 0.9, 2.0],
   "say": "So when b appends four, it changes that one shared list. And a sees the change too."},
  {"title": [{"text": "The Fix", "box": "yellow"}, {"text": "b = a.copy()", "box": "red"}],
   "image": {"type": "refs", "names": ["a", "b"], "boxes": [["1", "2", "3"], ["1", "2", "3", "4"]],
             "links": [[0, 0], [1, 1]], "new": [[1, 3]], "label": "TWO LISTS"},
   "face": "happy", "palette": "orange",
   "say": "To get a real copy, write b equals a dot copy. Now a and b are two different lists, and a stays one, two, three."},
  {"title": [{"text": "Remember", "box": "yellow"}, {"text": "this!", "color": "yellow"}],
   "image": {"type": "check", "items": ["b = a  ->  same list", "b = a.copy()  ->  new list", "list(a) or a[:] also copy"]},
